    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d156">

                <pb facs="0161" n="149" xml:id="pg149"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.01/381: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador to the Greek Government in Exile</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-31T09:00:00+03:00">August 31, 1943—9
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:17 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Greek Series 52. My Greek Series 42, August 18, 11 a.m. I assume that the
                    Department is aware of the fact that Churchill’s reply to the King was received
                    here via London on August 26.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
